    "body": "Welcome to Neginato Mezora Neginato Mezora is a native macOS meteorological workstation and hyper-local precipitation nowcasting application. It synthesizes up to 13 numerical weather prediction (NWP) models from five free, key-less upstream providers ( Open-Meteo , NOAA National Weather Service , MET Norway , DWD Bright Sky , and Environment Canada ) and fuses them with real-time physical airport METARs, DWD/KNMI 10-minute SYNOP observations, 90m DEM surface analysis, and US EPA AirNow + Copernicus CAMS/EEA air quality monitors. Quick Navigation Rain Graph & Bars Guide \u2014 Understand what the cyan bars (Rain rate, left axis) and amber-rose curve (Rain chance %, right axis) represent. Settings: Data Sources & Weights (\u2318,) \u2014 Configure enabled providers, inspect regional horizon profiles, and adjust per-source and per-model blend weights. Ensemble Blending & Citations \u2014 Full mathematical formulas, regional horizon weight tables, and academic references. Live Station 3D Assimilation \u2014 How nearby physical weather stations and air quality sensors are fused in real time. Key Features at a Glance Feature Description Labeled Dual-Series Rain Charts Side-by-side Next 2 hours (15-minute sub-hourly nowcast bars across US, Canada, UK, Netherlands, Germany, and Europe) and Next 24 hours (hourly bars + probability curve) with explicit series pills, left/right axis labels, peak callout badges, and interactive hover inspection. Regional 4-Band Ensemble Weights Automatic regional horizon profiles for the US, UK & Ireland, Netherlands & Benelux, Germany & Central Europe, Canada, Nordic & Baltic, Europe, and Worldwide. Open Settings (\u2318,) to inspect regional profiles and tune blend multipliers ( 0.00\u00d7 to 3.00\u00d7 ). 3D Live Station Assimilation Blends up to 16 NOAA/FAA AviationWeather METAR stations within 95 km plus NWS ASOS and DWD/KNMI Bright Sky 10-minute SYNOP observations using 3D anisotropic kernels, lapse-rate elevation correction, Shepard angular de-clustering, and MAD outlier QC. Street-Address & Pin Geocoding Search any street address, postal code, city, or raw lat, lon coordinates via 5 parallel geocoders or drop a pin on the interactive Apple Map."
